  ],
  "text": "Every current scenario for the end of the universe is strange, and none of them are settled. It comes down to one thing nobody understands. Dark energy. The expansion is not slowing down, the way gravity says it should. It is speeding up. Something is pushing, and we have essentially no idea what it is. If it stays as it is, you get heat death. Expansion continues and everything spreads out. Stars burn out, matter thins, and eventually nothing is close enough for anything to happen. If dark energy strengthens, you get the big rip. Galaxies come apart, then stars, then atoms. And if it ever reversed, everything falls back together into a big crunch. Current evidence points to continued expansion, which makes heat death the front runner. But all of it rests on something we cannot explain. This is a live frontier, not a forecast. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
